  "status": "formalized",
  "note": "`Contest.track` proves 𝔡 ≤ 2|δ|/b_* for two histories (`weightA` the maximum coordinate distance, `bonusB` the endpoint, b_* = brace 0) by first proving 𝔡 ≤ |δ|/b_* + 8·`glint`·𝔡 with `glint` = 1/128. On the series space `Amp.Beam` = ℓ¹ and for ‖e‖ ≤ (1/16)/4·brace_i, `Rally.danceN`, `Rally.danceD` and `Rally.payable` give ball preservation at radius `lux` = 1/16, contraction by 1/2 and the unique fixed point of `Rally.danceB` (the series map with its quadratic term), `Rally.south` and `Contest.score` identify its evaluations with the real recursion on the interval `Contest.ask` = 𝔍, and `Campaign.Winter.convergence` (proved in `Campaign.offers`) gives fixed-level convergence of couplings and activity coordinates for every convergent endpoint sequence.",
